1.3.6.text:
The gun is fired at an angle $\varphi$ to the horizon. Initial velocity of the projectile $v.$ The ground surface is horizontal. Find:
a) the horizontal and vertical projections of velocity as a function of time;
b) the dependence of the $x$ and $y$ coordinates on time;
c) the trajectory equation, i.e. the dependence of $y$ on $x$;
d) the flight time, the highest altitude and range of the projectile.

1.4.9.text:
The body hits the wall with velocity $v$ and angle $\alpha$ to the line perpendicular to the wall. Determine the velocity of the body after an elastic impact if the wall is:
a) stationary;
b) moving perpendicular to itself at a speed $w$ towards the body;
c) moving at an angle $\beta$ to the line perpendicular to it at a speed $w$ towards the body.

